saqUciDepA112.title:
Description of the processes regarding IFM trade instruction capture, IFM trade instruction processing, IFM trade instruction settlement. The description should at least cover the following four points:
(i) The depositary is clearly identifiable in all communications and exchanges of information in relation with its safekeeping obligations (please also provide the means used by the depositary to receive and send IFM trade instructions); 
(ii) Any inbound communication in regard to the UCI client account (e.g. IFM trade instruction, sub-custodian settlement confirmation) is clearly identifiable as being submitted to the depositary;
(iii) The records of all transactions in assets to be held in custody maintained by the depositary also help to build the positions held on UCI client account; and
(iv) The depositary is authorized to act on the UCI client cash accounts opened with third parties through which the cash flows relate to transactions in assets to be held in custody.

saqUciDepA2025234.title:
Do the depositary's ownership verification process and procedure described above:
 (a) cover the specific verifications to be performed for the various asset classes (private equity, real estate, fund of funds, etc.); and
 (b) include the following documentation to be at least obtained by the depositary and addressing the following objectives:
   (i) the fund's/IFM's decision to enter into the transaction;
   (ii) the existence of the transaction;
   (iii) the cost of the transaction;
   (iv) the existence of legal entities (SPVs) involved in the UCI's holding chain; and
   (v) the legal ownership risk (legal due diligence)?

saqPsd22024080.description:
3 possible scenarios:

1. “adapted PSU interface” (i.e. to allow the TPPs to use the interface also used by the PSUs to access their payment accounts (e.g. an e-banking website), with an adaptation of this interface to allow the TPPs to identify themselves towards the ASPSP);

2. "dedicated interface" (i.e. an interface that is dedicated to the communication with those TPPs and that shall offer at all times the same level of availability and performance, including support, as the interface(s) made available to the PSU for directly accessing its payment account online) with fallback mechanism exemption (as set out in Article 33 of the RTS);

3. "dedicated interface" (i.e. an interface that is dedicated to the communication with those TPPs and that shall offer at all times the same level of availability and performance, including support, as the interface(s) made available to the PSU for directly accessing its payment account online) without fallback mechanism exemption (as set out in Article 33 of the RTS).
